# Mini GPT from Scratch

A character-level GPT (decoder-only Transformer) built from scratch in PyTorch, following Andrej Karpathy's "Let's build GPT: from scratch, in code, spelled out". Trained on the Tiny Shakespeare dataset to generate Shakespeare-style text.

## Architecture
- Token embeddings + learned positional embeddings
- Multi-head causal self-attention (scaled dot-product, masked so tokens cannot see the future)
- Position-wise feed-forward network (4x expansion)
- Residual connections and LayerNorm in every block
- Final LayerNorm + linear head over the character vocabulary
- Trained with cross-entropy loss and the AdamW optimizer

**Model size:** 0.82M parameters (4 layers, 4 heads, 128-dim embeddings, context length 64)

## Project structure
```
mini-gpt/
├── gpt.py             # model, training loop, text generation
├── download.py        # downloads the Tiny Shakespeare dataset
├── input.txt          # dataset (created by download.py)
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

## How to run
```bash
pip install torch
python download.py
python gpt.py
```
Training runs on CPU in roughly 35-40 minutes with the default settings. For better results on a GPU, increase `n_embd`, `n_layer`, `block_size` and `max_iters` at the top of `gpt.py`.

